# Release bundles, and the whole directory.
#
# It used to track the .txt manifests. That made `releases/` a folder named
# exactly where a download lives, containing no download and a manifest for a
# build that no longer existed — reported by someone who went looking there to
# install the app, which is the one place it is reasonable to look. Nothing in
# it was worth the misdirection: the reasoning it held is in README's Install
# section, and the install path is a command rather than a file.
#
# make-release.sh still writes here for local archiving; it is simply not part
# of the repository any more.
releases/
